1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,940
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,340
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:16,650
Da Mi, what should I do?

4
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,120
CEO Jeon Jin Hee said...

5
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:22,530
she would no longer shop
at our department store.

6
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:27,570
I'm clearly to blame
for losing a VVIP client,

7
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:29,730
so they won't renew my contract.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,500
What do I do?

9
00:00:33,470 --> 00:00:37,040
There's no one else who can pay
my father's hospital bills.

10
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:45,080
(Episode 25)

11
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:52,520
Hello.

12
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:55,490
I'm Kang Da Mi, manager
at K Department Store's VIP Luxury Hall.

13
00:00:57,930 --> 00:00:59,930
I'm the CEO's designated
personal shopper.

14
00:01:00,530 --> 00:01:03,030
I came to see her
about an urgent matter.

15
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:04,770
Please let me in.

16
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,300
Do you have an appointment?

17
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:08,310
I don't,

18
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:12,410
but I'm not allowed
to contact the CEO first.

19
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:15,250
Still, I really need to see her.

20
00:01:15,810 --> 00:01:18,080
Could you please tell her I'm here?

21
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:21,450
I'm sorry,
but without an appointment,

22
00:01:21,450 --> 00:01:22,690
I can't let you in.

23
00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:24,190
Please, I'm begging you.

24
00:01:24,690 --> 00:01:27,730
Could you just call the CEO's office
and let her know I'm here...

25
00:01:28,090 --> 00:01:30,530
and would like to see her,
even briefly?

26
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:32,900
Isn't she...

27
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,500
the girl from the department store?

28
00:01:36,730 --> 00:01:38,540
I'm sorry, but I can't.

29
00:01:43,110 --> 00:01:44,180
Let her in.

30
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:48,950
Goodness...

31
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,350
She's also my personal shopper.

32
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,050
I'll let CEO Jeon know myself.

33
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:00,460
This is a surprise, Kang Da Mi.
How have you been?

34
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,730
Hello, sir.

35
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:05,300
I need to see CEO Jeon...

36
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:14,340
It sounds urgent,

37
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:18,140
but may I ask first
why you need to see CEO Jeon?

38
00:02:20,650 --> 00:02:23,820
You're Team Leader Cha Do Yun, right?

39
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:26,950
Yes. You have a good memory.

40
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:29,190
You're my client, after all.

41
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:32,560
Are you aware that recently,

42
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:34,230
the heel of a pair of shoes
CEO Jeon bought...

43
00:02:34,290 --> 00:02:35,460
from our boutique broke,

44
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,660
and she ended up getting injured?

45
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:41,070
- Yes.
- As the boutique manager,

46
00:02:41,270 --> 00:02:42,500
I came to see her about that...

47
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:44,940
because there's something
I must explain.

48
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,010
You said
you'd let me see her, right?

49
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:49,410
Please help me.

50
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:55,450
Sure, let's go up together.
I'll walk you to CEO Jeon's office.

51
00:02:55,450 --> 00:02:57,650
Really? Thank you, sir...

52
00:02:58,180 --> 00:02:59,720
I mean...

53
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:02,050
It's Team Leader Cha Do Yun.

54
00:03:03,990 --> 00:03:05,220
Yes, Team Leader Cha.

55
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:12,930
Good morning, Team Leader Cha.

56
00:03:13,770 --> 00:03:14,970
Assistant Manager Kang.

57
00:03:22,210 --> 00:03:23,210
Da Mi.

58
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:25,840
Pick it up.

59
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:29,750
- Excuse me?
- Pick it up and see for yourself.

60
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:32,750
If you're curious,
pick it up and see for yourself.

61
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:41,960
You're the department store
VIP showroom manager, right?

62
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,600
What was your name again?

63
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:46,060
Anyway, what brings you
to our company?

64
00:03:46,330 --> 00:03:50,540
She said she needed to see CEO Jeon.
I offered to escort her.

65
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:52,140
You personally, Team Leader Cha?

66
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,770
You and I are supposed to go
straight to the store...

67
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,840
where we're sponsoring outfits
and look around the site.

68
00:03:57,910 --> 00:03:58,980
That was our schedule
for this morning.

69
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:02,210
Assistant Manager Lee from PR
agreed to go with you instead,

70
00:04:02,350 --> 00:04:03,680
so you can head over first,
Assistant Manager Kang.

71
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:07,250
I'll join you by 11:00 a.m.
to look around.

72
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:08,790
What about the car, then?

73
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:10,120
I handed my car keys
to Assistant Manager Lee...

74
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,760
as soon as I arrived at work.

75
00:04:12,490 --> 00:04:13,760
Go upstairs and get ready.

76
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:16,660
All right, understood.

77
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:30,440
Shall we head up too?

78
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,280
Yes.

79
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,920
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

80
00:04:41,690 --> 00:04:43,350
How's the mood
at the company, honey?

81
00:04:43,790 --> 00:04:46,660
Do you really think Mother
is going to remove you as CEO?

82
00:04:47,030 --> 00:04:49,990
Don't you know how my mother is?

83
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,500
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

84
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:55,300
Are you saying she already notified
the executives?

85
00:04:56,830 --> 00:04:59,370
I'm sorting out the files
to hand over to the VP.

86
00:04:59,470 --> 00:05:00,640
(Hwanggeum Capital)

87
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:02,240
For now, I'll have to keep
a low profile...

88
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:04,210
and show her that
I'm reflecting on things.

89
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:06,480
Mother is really
crossing the line this time.

90
00:05:06,710 --> 00:05:10,210
It does feel like her mood swings
have grown worse lately.

91
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:11,650
(CEO Cha In Sung)

92
00:05:11,750 --> 00:05:14,220
Though she's always been
unpredictable.

93
00:05:15,790 --> 00:05:19,260
Right, today is my brother
and his wife's memorial day,

94
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:20,830
so you must be very busy.

95
00:05:22,130 --> 00:05:23,860
I need to head home
early to prepare.

96
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,330
I'm always so grateful
to you every year.

97
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:32,800
Also, Seung Yun said
he'd stop by the columbarium,

98
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:35,140
take care of some errands,
and come home tonight.

99
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:36,540
Is that so?

100
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,480
Starting this year,
your brother and sister-in-law...

101
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:40,710
must feel so proud.

102
00:05:41,150 --> 00:05:43,350
It'll be the first time
they receive an offering...

103
00:05:43,410 --> 00:05:44,920
from Seung Yun, who grew up so well.

104
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:47,450
Indeed.

105
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:49,520
I can't help thinking...

106
00:05:49,690 --> 00:05:51,590
how wonderful it would be
if they were still alive...

107
00:05:51,590 --> 00:05:53,390
and we were all living
under one roof.

108
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:57,860
I know.
Honey, I'll see you at home later.

109
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,330
All right, take care then.

110
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:03,670
(Beloved Jin Hee)

111
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:11,440
Long time no see.

112
00:06:11,510 --> 00:06:14,610
I've been out of my mind
looking for Da Mi lately.

113
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:16,150
Do you remember this photo?

114
00:06:16,450 --> 00:06:19,720
Luckily for me, I had a copy of it.

115
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:20,790
Get in touch.

116
00:06:30,730 --> 00:06:31,730
This can't be.

117
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,100
How does my aunt have this photo?

118
00:06:40,770 --> 00:06:41,770
Come in.

119
00:06:42,670 --> 00:06:43,670
Ma'am?

120
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,080
Yes.

121
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:54,220
Team Leader Cha.

122
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:55,850
What's going on?

123
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:58,660
Manager Kang had an urgent matter...

124
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,860
and needed to see you in person,
so when she came by,

125
00:07:00,930 --> 00:07:01,990
I brought her in.

126
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:05,400
Hello, CEO Jeon. I'm Kang Da Mi.

127
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:08,370
I sincerely apologize
for dropping by unannounced.

128
00:07:09,130 --> 00:07:11,240
I'm sure you have your reasons.

129
00:07:12,470 --> 00:07:13,470
Please, take a seat first.

130
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:26,820
- Have a seat.
- Thank you.

131
00:07:34,330 --> 00:07:37,260
Well, as you put it,

132
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,830
shall we hear the reason
you dropped by my office...

133
00:07:40,830 --> 00:07:42,000
so suddenly?

134
00:07:43,470 --> 00:07:46,400
I came to ask for
your leniency, ma'am.

135
00:07:47,670 --> 00:07:48,670
Leniency?

136
00:07:50,010 --> 00:07:51,010
Yes.

137
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:56,310
Well, what kind of leniency
do you expect from me, Manager Kang?

138
00:07:56,550 --> 00:07:57,820
Well, the thing is...

139
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:01,990
Ma'am, the reason Manager Kang
came to see you today...

140
00:08:02,050 --> 00:08:04,460
is regarding the broken heel
on the shoes...

141
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:07,120
- you purchased previously...
- Just a moment, Team Leader Cha.

142
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:10,700
I'll question you later about...

143
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:15,070
how you came to bring
Manager Kang into my office...

144
00:08:15,830 --> 00:08:17,130
without my consent or notice.

145
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:21,510
Manager Kang,
you must speak for yourself.

146
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,540
What's this leniency
you need from me?

147
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:26,740
Well...

148
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:40,560
It arrived right on time.
I was worried it might be late.

149
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:42,860
I was going to buy them myself
and head out,

150
00:08:43,230 --> 00:08:45,100
but Grandma told me
she had already ordered them.

151
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:48,030
Yes, she ordered them
a few days ago.

152
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:49,100
Here you go.

153
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:55,610
Wait, why are there two bouquets?

154
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:57,340
Yes.

155
00:08:58,310 --> 00:09:00,180
You'll need two.

156
00:09:01,650 --> 00:09:04,180
One for Mom and one for Dad,
right, Grandma?

157
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:05,850
No.

158
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:09,090
Your parents always
shared one bouquet.

159
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:11,020
They were so devoted to each other.

160
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:14,830
You'll understand the other one
once you get there.

161
00:09:15,730 --> 00:09:18,230
- Understood. I'll be on my way.
- Yes.

162
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,400
Seung Yun.

163
00:09:20,430 --> 00:09:23,100
- Yes?
- There's no need to rush back.

164
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:26,100
The memorial service
is late at night,

165
00:09:26,270 --> 00:09:27,710
so take your time coming home.

166
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:30,810
- Yes, I will.
- All right.

167
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:36,510
- Have a safe trip.
- Thanks.

168
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:43,820
Did you prepare
everything separately,

169
00:09:44,490 --> 00:09:45,990
just as I asked?

170
00:09:46,390 --> 00:09:47,390
Yes, Madam.

171
00:09:47,890 --> 00:09:49,790
But has CEO Jeon really been...

172
00:09:49,790 --> 00:09:51,360
setting the memorial table
every time?

173
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:52,760
She has.

174
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:55,100
And she's doing so again this year.

175
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:56,970
I'll quietly take care of it early,

176
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,270
just as you instructed.

177
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:02,110
Yes, I'm counting on you.

178
00:10:13,650 --> 00:10:14,720
Jun Sung.

179
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,220
My dear daughter-in-law.

180
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:25,330
I'm sorry to hear that the employee
who repaired my shoes...

181
00:10:25,730 --> 00:10:27,000
won't have her contract renewed.

182
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,200
However, Manager Kang.

183
00:10:29,830 --> 00:10:30,840
Yes, ma'am.

184
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:32,900
The way you're
speaking and acting...

185
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:35,540
makes it sound like
I told the department store...

186
00:10:35,540 --> 00:10:37,240
to fire her right away...

187
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:40,540
or I'd take my business elsewhere,

188
00:10:40,610 --> 00:10:42,680
as if I made some sort of threat.

189
00:10:43,410 --> 00:10:44,550
I find that rather offensive.

190
00:10:45,950 --> 00:10:49,290
I'm truly sorry
if it sounded that way.

191
00:10:49,950 --> 00:10:54,560
However, according to our manager,
you stated that because of this,

192
00:10:54,630 --> 00:10:57,860
you would no longer shop
at our department store.

193
00:10:58,330 --> 00:11:00,030
Because of that,

194
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:01,500
since we're losing
a valuable client,

195
00:11:01,570 --> 00:11:04,070
they said they had no choice...

196
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:05,740
but to hold my employee,
Song Min Hee, accountable.

197
00:11:06,870 --> 00:11:11,480
So I thought if you would be so kind
as to show some leniency,

198
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:14,550
- she could keep her job...
- Hold on.

199
00:11:15,510 --> 00:11:18,180
I made it very clear
to the department store...

200
00:11:18,180 --> 00:11:19,520
that I didn't want any action taken.

201
00:11:20,350 --> 00:11:22,590
I simply exercised my right
as a customer,

202
00:11:22,650 --> 00:11:26,090
however small it may be,
to take my business elsewhere...

203
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:30,060
because I wasn't satisfied
with the service.

204
00:11:30,930 --> 00:11:34,200
So if you're looking for leniency,

205
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:37,440
shouldn't you ask the manager
at the department store instead of me?

206
00:11:37,700 --> 00:11:38,870
Don't you agree?

207
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:44,740
Still, CEO Jeon,
if you could just make a phone call,

208
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,640
- the department store would...
- Team Leader Cha.

209
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:47,880
Aren't you busy?

210
00:11:48,810 --> 00:11:50,650
I thought you were swamped...

211
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:52,320
planning the launch
for early next year.

212
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:55,320
Please get back to work.

213
00:12:00,790 --> 00:12:03,190
Excuse me, but I should get going.

214
00:12:16,310 --> 00:12:17,610
I'm terribly sorry about this.

215
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:21,110
I should at least offer you
a cup of tea, Manager Kang,

216
00:12:21,650 --> 00:12:24,880
but I have to head home right after
wrapping up my morning work.

217
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:29,020
Not at all.

218
00:12:29,090 --> 00:12:31,260
Thank you for taking the time
to speak with me.

219
00:12:31,690 --> 00:12:32,920
I'll take my leave now.

220
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:35,290
Kang Da Mi.

221
00:12:35,990 --> 00:12:36,990
Yes?

222
00:12:37,530 --> 00:12:38,900
Last time, when I asked...

223
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:44,070
if you didn't care about tomorrow,
you replied, "Yes, I suppose so."

224
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:45,640
Do you remember that?

225
00:12:47,170 --> 00:12:48,340
Yes, ma'am.

226
00:12:49,910 --> 00:12:52,540
It's admirable that you're fighting
for your junior colleague's job,

227
00:12:52,910 --> 00:12:55,250
but from now on, you'd better look
where you're leaping...

228
00:12:55,250 --> 00:12:56,580
before charging ahead.

229
00:12:57,850 --> 00:13:00,120
This is as far as my kindness...

230
00:13:01,250 --> 00:13:02,350
toward you goes.

231
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:06,260
I understand.

232
00:13:17,370 --> 00:13:18,700
Barging into my company?

233
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:21,070
She certainly is bold.

234
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,840
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

235
00:13:26,010 --> 00:13:28,010
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

236
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:45,400
Even if you're alive
out there somewhere,

237
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:48,430
you...

238
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:51,970
must never show up in my life again.

239
00:13:54,310 --> 00:13:55,340
Never.

240
00:14:07,550 --> 00:14:08,590
Kang Da Mi.

241
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:14,120
Your talk with CEO Jeon
didn't go well, did it?

242
00:14:15,290 --> 00:14:16,330
No, it didn't.

243
00:14:16,690 --> 00:14:18,800
- Still...
- Still?

244
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:22,430
She wasn't wrong about anything,
so I couldn't say much back.

245
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:27,570
I was just thinking,
a company's CEO really is...

246
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:29,310
on another level.

247
00:14:31,110 --> 00:14:33,580
Thank you for helping me today,
Team Leader Cha.

248
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:35,880
It was really nothing.

249
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:40,320
I wish things had gone better.
I'm sorry.

250
00:14:41,250 --> 00:14:45,390
Actually, I went to your store
because I had a favor to ask,

251
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:47,790
but you were on leave,
so I missed you.

252
00:14:48,090 --> 00:14:50,630
A favor for me? What is it?

253
00:14:51,730 --> 00:14:53,530
Now is probably not the best time.

254
00:14:53,730 --> 00:14:55,230
You should head back to the store...

255
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:57,600
and look into
your colleague's situation first.

256
00:14:58,270 --> 00:15:00,370
I have your number,
so I'll reach out.

257
00:15:01,510 --> 00:15:02,810
All right, see you then.

258
00:15:08,050 --> 00:15:10,680
You have to do me this favor, okay?

259
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:25,760
What could a team leader
at such a huge company...

260
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:26,830
possibly need from me?

261
00:15:29,270 --> 00:15:30,930
Anyway, Min Hee...

262
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:32,670
Song Min Hee...

263
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:45,050
(Kim Hyun Jung, Cha Jun Sung)

264
00:16:04,370 --> 00:16:05,540
(Gong Hye Ji, Ju Ni)

265
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,040
(The late Ju Ni, Born July 8, 1998,
Died October 13, 2003)

266
00:16:12,010 --> 00:16:13,010
Son.

267
00:16:14,610 --> 00:16:16,450
Why have you been going
to work so late lately?

268
00:16:16,710 --> 00:16:18,520
You used to leave
at the crack of dawn every day.

269
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:21,950
Mom. I'm a manager now.

270
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:26,860
I've been there for years.
If a manager shows up too early,

271
00:16:27,190 --> 00:16:28,690
the team hates it.

272
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:31,060
Is that so?

273
00:16:31,330 --> 00:16:32,330
Yes.

274
00:16:32,930 --> 00:16:33,930
I'm heading out.

275
00:16:34,530 --> 00:16:35,530
Wait.

276
00:16:37,170 --> 00:16:38,340
Sit down for a second.

277
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:50,610
Why?

278
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:52,620
I need to get to work.

279
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,220
Da Mi told me yesterday...

280
00:16:58,260 --> 00:17:00,290
that you got the urgent cash
from your company?

281
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:04,260
- Yes, pretty much.
- Pretty much?

282
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:08,030
You said you needed 200,000
or 300,000 dollars right away.

283
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:10,230
Are you still short?

284
00:17:10,770 --> 00:17:11,840
If I tell you,

285
00:17:12,470 --> 00:17:15,240
- are you going to help me, Mom?
- Just answer my question.

286
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:20,610
You're short, aren't you? How much?

287
00:17:22,610 --> 00:17:24,280
I'm short about 80,000 dollars.

288
00:17:27,850 --> 00:17:29,020
With that money,

289
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:32,590
can you pay back the rest slowly
while working at the company?

290
00:17:34,490 --> 00:17:35,590
I'll have to.

291
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:48,170
- What's this?
- Eighty thousand dollars.

292
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:50,340
Mom,

293
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:52,710
how did you know
I was short 80,000 dollars?

294
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:55,150
Did Da Mi tell you?

295
00:17:56,550 --> 00:17:58,520
What would Da Mi know to tell me?

296
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:00,780
This is all I can do for you.

297
00:18:02,450 --> 00:18:03,490
But...

298
00:18:05,690 --> 00:18:06,960
I'm not just giving it to you.

299
00:18:07,590 --> 00:18:08,760
No matter how many years it takes,

300
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:12,160
you absolutely must pay me back
every cent of this money.

301
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,430
Do you understand?

302
00:18:16,530 --> 00:18:17,870
Do I really have to pay it back?

303
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:23,140
- Give it back if you don't want to.
- No. I'll pay you back.

304
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:26,310
I'm off to work.

305
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:30,980
You must pay me back that money.

306
00:18:44,630 --> 00:18:46,730
My stomach is in knots, seriously.

307
00:18:59,910 --> 00:19:01,150
I knew it.

308
00:19:02,010 --> 00:19:03,850
There's no way my mom
would turn her back on me.

309
00:19:21,630 --> 00:19:22,630
What is this?

310
00:19:23,330 --> 00:19:25,600
I deposited
three months' interest yesterday.

311
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:27,200
Yes, sir.

312
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:28,870
As a token of my gratitude
and support,

313
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:30,610
I went to my favorite cafe...

314
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:32,510
and brought you
freshly brewed coffee...

315
00:19:32,610 --> 00:19:33,740
made with fresh beans.

316
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:35,950
You must have had a hard time
getting the money together.

317
00:19:36,010 --> 00:19:37,450
Thank you so very much.

318
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:42,550
Do secondary lenders
deliver coffee now...

319
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:43,850
when clients pay overdue interest?

320
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:45,760
I had no idea.

321
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,430
Thanks for the coffee. Goodbye.

322
00:19:48,830 --> 00:19:49,830
Sir!

323
00:19:53,730 --> 00:19:55,530
Could you please tell us...

324
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:57,500
your repayment plan
for the overdue principal?

325
00:19:58,770 --> 00:20:00,670
Can't you see I'm leaving for work?

326
00:20:01,410 --> 00:20:03,610
I do. I can tell.

327
00:20:04,270 --> 00:20:05,480
Then could we set up a time...

328
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:07,180
for a consultation
over the phone later?

329
00:20:08,250 --> 00:20:09,280
Sure, let's do that.

330
00:20:13,780 --> 00:20:16,090
By the way, how old are you,
Ms. Cha Se Na?

331
00:20:16,450 --> 00:20:17,450
Me?

332
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:19,420
I'm 29.

333
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:21,960
You're really 29?

334
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:27,330
I do look a bit young for my age.
Good genes run in our family.

335
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:29,930
Twenty-nine...

336
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:33,770
I'll make a repayment plan
and call you.

337
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:35,810
I'm begging you,

338
00:20:36,470 --> 00:20:38,410
please don't come
to my house anymore.

339
00:20:40,180 --> 00:20:43,050
Have a wonderful day
and make lots of money, sir.

340
00:20:48,190 --> 00:20:49,720
Once I collect the principal
from you,

341
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:52,160
Grandma promised to set up
my own business for me.

342
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:54,830
You're totally trapped in my net.

343
00:20:55,890 --> 00:20:57,330
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

344
00:20:57,330 --> 00:20:58,630
Yes, here you go.

345
00:20:58,700 --> 00:21:00,630
Excuse me, could we get
more pickled onions?

346
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:02,370
- Sure.
- Pack one ginseng chicken soup...

347
00:21:02,370 --> 00:21:04,300
- to go, please.
- Sure.

348
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:09,810
Hey, where did Mrs. Choi go?
My feet are killing me.

349
00:21:09,870 --> 00:21:11,380
They feel like they're on fire.

350
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:12,880
I don't know.

351
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:15,210
Is her leg acting up again?

352
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:17,450
She didn't say anything
to me either.

353
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:20,580
Hey.

354
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,620
- Yes?
- Take this to table three.

355
00:21:22,890 --> 00:21:25,290
Got it. Gosh.

356
00:21:26,990 --> 00:21:28,260
Here you go.

357
00:21:37,730 --> 00:21:38,770
Darn it.

358
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:40,670
I bust my back all day,
but when I get home,

359
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:42,110
no one is even here to greet me.

360
00:21:44,110 --> 00:21:46,980
Right. My wife went to work.

361
00:21:48,110 --> 00:21:50,010
Well, even when she is home,

362
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:53,050
I can count on one hand the times
she made me a proper meal.

363
00:21:55,220 --> 00:21:56,790
Goodness, let's see...

364
00:21:58,890 --> 00:22:03,590
This darn rice paddle
still has dried rice stuck to it.

365
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:06,660
Unbelievable.

366
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:10,500
There isn't even any rice left,
so why is it sitting on warm?

367
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:16,240
Wait a second.

368
00:22:23,010 --> 00:22:24,010
What's that?

369
00:22:25,050 --> 00:22:26,050
Who is that?

370
00:22:29,790 --> 00:22:30,790
Who is it?

371
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:33,290
I asked who was out there.

372
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:34,560
Open up!

373
00:22:39,930 --> 00:22:42,230
Goodness, Mom.

374
00:22:50,070 --> 00:22:52,180
Eat it or toss it,
do whatever you want.

375
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:57,250
You told me to never
show my face again,

376
00:22:57,710 --> 00:22:58,980
so why did you come here?

377
00:23:02,750 --> 00:23:06,120
I came to ask why you returned
looking like such a mess.

378
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:09,430
- Pardon?
- What were you hoping for,

379
00:23:09,430 --> 00:23:11,060
moving to this neighborhood?

380
00:23:12,060 --> 00:23:14,560
Do you have no pride as a man?

381
00:23:16,970 --> 00:23:19,400
Stop gaping like a goldfish
and answer me.

382
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:20,640
Your mother is asking you.

383
00:23:25,380 --> 00:23:26,680
Because I missed you.

384
00:23:31,550 --> 00:23:32,550
Ever since...

385
00:23:35,190 --> 00:23:36,520
you walked out like that,

386
00:23:36,590 --> 00:23:38,790
I haven't been able
to hold my head high...

387
00:23:39,290 --> 00:23:41,190
for a single second.

388
00:23:45,300 --> 00:23:46,660
Just don't get caught.

389
00:23:47,330 --> 00:23:48,870
Goodness!

390
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:51,170
Mother.

391
00:23:55,170 --> 00:23:57,210
What brings you here?

392
00:23:57,910 --> 00:24:01,180
Why isn't there a single soul
living in this house?

393
00:24:04,250 --> 00:24:05,520
Mom...

394
00:24:09,550 --> 00:24:10,590
Did you hear that?

395
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:12,860
She sees the two of us
standing right here,

396
00:24:12,860 --> 00:24:14,190
and she claims there's nobody home.

397
00:24:15,190 --> 00:24:17,260
She's totally mocking us, isn't she?

398
00:24:23,430 --> 00:24:24,430
Mom.

399
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:27,240
Honey!

400
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:33,910
Mom.

401
00:24:48,790 --> 00:24:50,160
Hey, wait. Stop.

402
00:24:54,930 --> 00:24:55,930
What are you doing?

403
00:24:56,670 --> 00:24:57,800
Sneaking around like a cat?

404
00:25:00,070 --> 00:25:02,110
I brought back the side dish
containers your mom gave me.

405
00:25:02,570 --> 00:25:03,570
Give them to her.

406
00:25:04,070 --> 00:25:05,140
What's in that cloth bundle?

407
00:25:06,080 --> 00:25:07,080
That's...

408
00:25:08,210 --> 00:25:09,210
reishi mushrooms.

409
00:25:09,710 --> 00:25:11,380
They say it's good
for neuralgia in the elderly.

410
00:25:11,580 --> 00:25:13,480
Brew it and have her drink it
often like water.

411
00:25:13,750 --> 00:25:15,090
Goodness.

412
00:25:15,790 --> 00:25:18,490
I thought you worked three shifts.
Are you off today?

413
00:25:20,290 --> 00:25:21,290
What if I am?

414
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:22,690
Buy me a cup of coffee.

415
00:25:24,760 --> 00:25:26,160
Even if I had money to burn,

416
00:25:26,230 --> 00:25:28,730
there's no way I'd ever sit down
and drink coffee with you again.

417
00:25:29,270 --> 00:25:31,530
Then let's just go to the playground
and talk for a bit.

418
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:40,180
The clinic is a bit more...

419
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:43,110
Cozy than you expected?

420
00:25:43,480 --> 00:25:44,510
No, not that.

421
00:25:45,320 --> 00:25:48,690
Seeing you here, Dr. Ju,
you look really at peace.

422
00:25:50,450 --> 00:25:51,720
I wanted to feel that way,

423
00:25:52,060 --> 00:25:55,660
and I felt I could do that here,
so I opened my clinic in this spot.

424
00:25:56,660 --> 00:26:00,960
My wife and daughter
would've been so grateful today.

425
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:03,670
Thank you for the flowers.

426
00:26:06,040 --> 00:26:07,870
Grandma prepared those for you.

427
00:26:10,440 --> 00:26:13,180
Dr. Ju, I really must ask you
something today.

428
00:26:15,650 --> 00:26:17,250
How did your connection...

429
00:26:17,850 --> 00:26:19,320
with my grandmother even begin?

430
00:26:22,020 --> 00:26:24,720
Before we get to that,
neither of us has had lunch yet.

431
00:26:25,220 --> 00:26:27,520
One of my favorite spots
is right across the street.

432
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:29,090
Let's go together, Seung Yun.

433
00:26:29,760 --> 00:26:30,760
All right.

434
00:26:37,630 --> 00:26:39,070
Dr. Ju, I'm really sorry,

435
00:26:39,170 --> 00:26:40,870
but would you mind
if I took this call?

436
00:26:41,070 --> 00:26:43,770
Of course. Go right ahead.
I'll wait outside.

437
00:26:50,250 --> 00:26:51,350
Hello, this is Cha Seung Yun.

438
00:26:52,450 --> 00:26:53,720
Hello, sir.

439
00:26:54,080 --> 00:26:55,850
This is Manager Kang Da Mi.

440
00:26:56,590 --> 00:26:58,720
I'm sorry I couldn't take
your call properly yesterday.

441
00:26:59,560 --> 00:27:01,890
May I ask
what you were calling about?

442
00:27:02,730 --> 00:27:03,760
Well, the thing is...

443
00:27:04,630 --> 00:27:06,860
There was something I wanted
to give to you in person, Da Mi.

444
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:10,730
If this is related to business,
I'm afraid, sir...

445
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:12,300
Yes?

446
00:27:12,770 --> 00:27:16,340
I no longer work
at the department store,

447
00:27:16,740 --> 00:27:18,680
so there's nothing further
I can assist with.

448
00:27:19,140 --> 00:27:20,140
I apologize.

449
00:27:20,810 --> 00:27:22,080
Wait, what do you mean?

450
00:27:22,680 --> 00:27:24,410
Are you saying you quit working
at the department store?

451
00:27:27,450 --> 00:27:28,490
Yes, sir.

452
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:31,890
As of today, I've resigned
from the department store.

453
00:27:35,890 --> 00:27:37,860
May I ask what happened?

454
00:27:38,130 --> 00:27:39,530
No. It's a personal matter.

455
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:42,570
Thank you for everything. Goodbye.

456
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:44,770
Kang Da Mi...

457
00:28:07,090 --> 00:28:08,960
(Mission: Mompossible)

458
00:28:09,130 --> 00:28:12,900
How will you explain to Ye Ri
that she suddenly has a grandma?

459
00:28:13,030 --> 00:28:15,170
Nothing stays a secret
forever in this world.

460
00:28:15,330 --> 00:28:16,330
What?

461
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:19,040
What on earth did I do today?

462
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:21,670
- What's this?
- From your perspective, Da Mi,

463
00:28:21,770 --> 00:28:23,010
this isn't a bad offer.

464
00:28:24,210 --> 00:28:26,180
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
